Third-party binaries
====================

bin/MINI 60 HE MAX_V1.52.exe is a vendor artifact: the SONiX USB MCU ISP tool,
rebranded by FINDER (Dongguan) Technology Co., Ltd., EV-signed and published for
updating Mini60HE Max keyboards. It is NOT covered by the MIT license in
LICENSE. Copyright and all rights remain with its authors, and its presence here
implies no affiliation with or endorsement by them.

It is kept in the repository only because the analysis scripts need the exact
file: they verify its SHA-256 pin (958A3995...3512D6) and extract the firmware
image they study from it. If you clone this repository and do not want the
binary, delete bin/ - nothing under docs/ depends on it, and the scripts that do
will stop at their SHA-256 check with a clear message.

Everything else in this repository - the analysis scripts, the documentation and
the findings written in them - is MIT licensed, see LICENSE.

